{"game": "palworld", "language": "english", "appid": 1623730, "month": "2026-04", "window": 3, "start_date": 1776297600, "end_date": 1776902399, "month_true_total": 1087, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-07 17:00:15 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "223878139", "author": {"steamid": "76561198204887881", "personaname": "DarkNidoking", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/DarkNidoking/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 16, "playtime_forever": 17156, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 11183, "last_played": 1783920623, "avatar": "df4a05aab4187c5cce8ef27a4a1319745275b1fb"}, "language": "english", "review": "in my 186 hours of playing Palworld, something about it just didn't feel right to me, but i was having so much fun doing stuff and playing with the pals. This game has allowed me to get some real enjoyment from the \"monster tamer\" genre, though it is not a true monster tamer game. While that is a major selling point for Palworld, you have the freedom to use whichever of the pals you want, and some of them are better than others if your interested in participating in the action or if your looking for that Monster Tamer experience. The boss's feel real cheap and unfair to fight, your normally alot weaker than whatever pal you go to make use of. I love that the fight puts more involvement on your part, but i don't like how Herbil is currently the only pal that seemingly matters, and players think he's a \"noob trap\" but i assure you your pals do nothing when you die and there's only so much you can to to stay alive. And you can wreck everything with the M2 grenades. There are WAY too many systems meant to improve your pals capabilities, playing this game as a \"monster tamer\" is almost too much more effort than just using a Wixen and a bunch of Gobfins and playing like it's GTA. And the boss's don't have that handicap, and aren't effected like you are if you were mounted on a pal. You can't currently transfer any Pals from one save file to another, not without potentially violating TOS. Allowed me to destress from the horrible experience i had in ARK and have a more pleasant experience. Even if i'm only playing single player. i came for a monster tamer, and Palworld feels like it wants to be like GTA more than Pokemon. Having played Palword and Pokemon, i don't know why nintendo was so concerned about this game. ", "timestamp_created": 1776902383, "timestamp_updated": 1777703459, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1705651175", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "223877478", "author": {"steamid": "76561198758046315", "personaname": "♯ ⋮  𝄞 MCNUGGETS ༉  .", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198758046315/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 1, "playtime_forever": 7079, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 4738, "last_played": 1785778670, "avatar": "2da4242378b0528893a86b3aef1d2801833454af"}, "language": "english", "review": "good\r\n", "timestamp_created": 1776901428, "timestamp_updated": 1776901428, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1705651175", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "223876427", "author": {"steamid": "76561199266997149", "personaname": "michaeljrosin", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199266997149/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 4, "playtime_forever": 14553, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 4480, "last_played": 1789557420, "avatar": "fef49